# ProtonForge test lab — configuration
#
# Copy to lab.env and uncomment what you need. Nothing here is required; every
# value below is the default the lab already uses.
#
# Precedence is environment > lab.env > defaults, so a one-off override does not
# need this file at all:
#
#     LAB_DISTROS=debian:trixie tests/steam-lab/steamlab test 20_deb_install
#
# lab.env is gitignored. Nothing in this lab needs a Steam account, and no case
# will ever ask for one — if you find yourself wanting to put credentials here,
# that is a bug in the lab.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- paths

# Where the lab keeps its work. Deliberately outside the repository: it fills up
# with a package per distribution and, if the Flatpak tier is used, a ~1.5 GB
# runtime.
#PF_LAB_DIR="$HOME/.cache/protonforge-testlab"

# The binary under test. Left empty, the lab looks for
# cmake-build-debug/ProtonForge, then cmake-build-release/ProtonForge, then
# /usr/bin/protonforge — so pointing this at the last one tests an installed
# package instead of a build tree.
#PF_BIN=""

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ selection

# Narrow the distribution matrix. Space separated; the names have to match
# LAB_DISTROS_DEFAULT in lib/docker.sh.
#LAB_DISTROS="debian:trixie ubuntu:26.04"

# Let the cases that reach the internet run. Off by default because 80_proton_mgr
# downloads a Proton build and GitHub allows 60 unauthenticated API requests an
# hour per address.
#LAB_TEST_NETWORK=0

# A GitHub personal access token, only used by 80_proton_mgr to raise that limit.
# Needs no scopes — public release data is all it reads.
#LAB_GITHUB_TOKEN=""

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- docker

# Network for the container cases. "none" by default, which is what makes them
# deterministic: no Steam CDN artwork, no ProtonDB, no GitHub. Set to "bridge" if
# you are debugging something that genuinely needs to reach out.
#LAB_DOCKER_NET=none

# Prefix for the images the lab builds.
#LAB_DOCKER_PREFIX=protonforge-lab

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- gui

# Size of the virtual screen. 1280x800 is deliberately small — it is the size
# where a window that does not fit is a real complaint rather than a theoretical
# one.
#LAB_GUI_WIDTH=1280
#LAB_GUI_HEIGHT=800

# The window manager. One is not optional: without it nothing has input focus and
# WM_NORMAL_HINTS is not enforced, which would make both the keyboard and the
# minimum-size assertions meaningless.
#LAB_GUI_WM=openbox

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- flatpak

# Build and run the Flatpak inside a privileged container instead of on the host.
# The host is the default because Flatpak needs bubblewrap, and bubblewrap needs
# privileges a normal container does not have — see the note at the top of
# lib/flatpak.sh. Either way the installation is isolated in $PF_LAB_DIR/flatpak
# and your own --user installs are untouched.
#LAB_FLATPAK_DOCKER=0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ appimage

# 76_appimage has no host mode to offer: build-appimage.sh containerises itself,
# and the artifact is then run in an image built from docker/appimage/Dockerfile —
# a distribution with what an AppImage may expect from a host and no Qt. Both are
# only worth changing to try another distribution.
#LAB_APPIMAGE_HOST_IMAGE=debian:bookworm
#PROTONFORGE_APPIMAGE_IMAGE=debian:bookworm

# Rebuild the AppImage build image even when it looks current. The digest check
# catches an edited Dockerfile or tools.env on its own; this is for when apt has
# newer packages and you want them.
#PROTONFORGE_APPIMAGE_REBUILD=0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ timeouts

#TIMEOUT_BUILD=1800     # a full release build inside a container
#TIMEOUT_CLI=60         # one CLI invocation
#TIMEOUT_GUI=25         # waiting for a window to appear
#TIMEOUT_LAUNCH=30      # waiting for a launched game
#TIMEOUT_FLATPAK=3600   # flatpak-builder, including the runtime download
